cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite the accompanying paper."
title: "Explicit evaluation of Sprung's half-logarithm H-matrix at X=0 for p=2 supersingular reduction"
authors:
  - family-names: Elkuch
    given-names: Raphael
    email: relkuch@gmail.com
type: software
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-05-25"
abstract: >-
  Verification code and data for the paper "Explicit evaluation of Sprung's
  half-logarithm H-matrix at X=0 for p=2 supersingular reduction". The code
  uses SageMath 10 to verify, bit-exactly, an explicit conversion bridge
  between SageMath's Dieudonné basis and Sprung's canonical basis on 180
  elliptic curves drawn from the Cremona database with conductors in
  [37, 63096].
keywords:
  - elliptic curves
  - p-adic L-functions
  - Iwasawa theory
  - supersingular reduction
  - Sprung half-logarithms
  - SageMath
  - Cremona database
